{# Widget "export" — Export & reporting (PL·18), off by default; the "Coverage &
   effort" direction turns it on.

   THE FILE AND THE SCREEN ALWAYS AGREE. The card states the row count of the
   month on screen BEFORE anything is asked for, from the SAME figures the KPI
   strip shows (dashboard.monthCount / monthDistanceKm) — so nobody discovers at
   the printer that they exported a different month than the one they were reading.

   TWO OF THE THREE DELIVERIES ARE REAL. The log as CSV and the tracks as GPX are
   one route in two formats (patrol_export), and both links carry the filter this
   card is describing. The queued monthly PDF needs a report pipeline this module
   does not have, so it is still marked pending rather than drawn as a dead
   button. #}
<div class="c">
    <span class="tab">Export &amp; reporting<span class="src">· carries the current filter</span></span>
    <div class="use patrol-ao-lead">Filter in force: <b>{{ filter.type ? types[filter.type].label|default(filter.type)|lower : 'all types' }} · {{ filter.station ? dashboard.stations[filter.station]|default(filter.station) : 'every station' }} · {{ (month|default(now))|date('F Y')|lower }}</b> — <b>{{ dashboard.monthCount|number_format }} {{ dashboard.monthCount == 1 ? 'patrol' : 'patrols' }}</b>.</div>

    <div class="patrol-exp">
        <span class="patrol-exp-t">Patrol log · CSV<em>{{ dashboard.monthCount|number_format }} rows · the log’s own columns, in the log’s own order</em></span>
        <a class="open-btn" href="{{ path('patrol_export', {uuid: area.uuid, _format: 'csv'}|merge(filter.toQuery)) }}">Download →</a>
    </div>
    <div class="patrol-exp">
        <span class="patrol-exp-t">Tracks · GPX<em>{{ dashboard.monthDistanceKm|number_format }} km · one &lt;trk&gt; per patrol, ids preserved</em></span>
        <a class="open-btn" href="{{ path('patrol_export', {uuid: area.uuid, _format: 'gpx'}|merge(filter.toQuery)) }}">Download →</a>
    </div>
    <div class="patrol-exp">
        <span class="patrol-exp-t">Monthly coverage report · PDF<em>the map, the two charts and the coverage table · queued, arrives by email</em></span>
        <span class="chip idle patrol-exp-soon">not wired yet</span>
    </div>
    <div class="patrol-stamp">Both files carry the filter above, unchanged. The monthly report is not built yet.</div>
</div>
